From e45635736cbd752587de9ea9ac9bd5bc0e919975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shine5402 <14089306+shine5402@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:47:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Allow keeping a RenderWidgetHost from being hidden

Ported from Electron's patches/chromium/disable_hidden.patch (originally
by Cheng Zhao), which Electron uses for its webPreferences
backgroundThrottling option.

Add RenderWidgetHostImpl::disable_hidden_. While it is set, WasHidden()
leaves the widget shown, so the renderer keeps producing frames and its
process, which has a shown widget, is not backgrounded.

Electron's changes to RenderWidgetHostViewAura are left out: Qt
WebEngine does not use that view, and does the equivalent in its own.
The default, false, leaves Chromium's behavior unchanged.
